# The tool versions a deploy expects on the box — the set the repository
# gate runs against. One tab-separated line per tool: name, the command
# that reports its version, and the token that must appear in the first
# line of that command's output. `any` records an accepted divergence: the
# observed version is reported, never failing the preflight — absence of
# the tool still fails it. Update a line when the gate's own toolchain
# moves; a deploy onto a box whose versions drift instead stops loudly
# before anything is installed (see install-review-runtime).
jq	jq --version	jq-1.8.2
node	node --version	v24.14.0
go	go version	go1.27.0
git	git --version	any
openssl	openssl version	any
claude	claude --version	2.1.251
codex	codex --version	codex-cli 0.151.0
